{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Are you jealous for me, etc.</b> According to the view of the one who says they were from the seventy, it intends in this manner: ״Are you jealous for the sake of my honor, that the men did not wish to come and receive the prophecy from me? Would that all the people of HaShem were prophets, and they would not receive prophecy from me but from HaShem,״ as it were. And it is the statement <b>when YHWH gives His spirit upon them</b> without Moses' mediation, for there is the source of humility and the firm resolution of the absence of zealousness. And according to the view of the one who says [they were] from the designated ones, it intends in this manner: ״Are you jealous for me״ — meaning, for my statements that I made [concerning] seventy, and seventy [plus] two prophesied — ״Would that״ etc., and the reason <b>when YHWH gives</b> etc. — meaning that the seventy whom HaShem said would be infused from the spirit of Moses was at the outset, before HaShem began to grant prophecy to others besides Moses. But after HaShem bestowed the spirit of Moses and gave it to the seventy, prophecy was permitted to all — <b>when YHWH gives His spirit upon them</b> — and there is no negation here of Moses' prophecy."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:57.905441343Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}